From: umurmur-esp32 <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] ssli_mbedtls: map PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY to ZERO_RETURN

Non-upstreamable (ESP-only for now).

On ESP-IDF mbedTLS 4.1.0, PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY -> immediate Client_free
drains free heap when other TLS sessions are alive (~200 B/cycle).
Desktop mbedTLS 4.2.0 does not reproduce under valgrind; keep this as
an ESP carry until IDF's mbedtls is newer or the root cause is clearer.

Maps peer close_notify to SSLI_ERROR_ZERO_RETURN so Client_read takes
the Client_close path (OpenSSL parity).

diff --git a/src/ssli_mbedtls.c b/src/ssli_mbedtls.c
index 5957b35..32cfdb6 100644
--- a/src/ssli_mbedtls.c
+++ b/src/ssli_mbedtls.c
@@ -430,6 +430,9 @@ int SSLi_write(SSL_handle_t *ssl, uint8_t *buf, int len)
 int SSLi_get_error(SSL_handle_t *ssl, int code)
 {
 	(void)ssl;
+	/* ESP-only: PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY -> ZERO_RETURN (see patch header). */
+	if (code == MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY)
+		return SSLI_ERROR_ZERO_RETURN;
 	return code;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/ssli_mbedtls4.c b/src/ssli_mbedtls4.c
index 6f8a3dd..2238bbc 100644
--- a/src/ssli_mbedtls4.c
+++ b/src/ssli_mbedtls4.c
@@ -222,6 +222,9 @@ int SSLi_write(SSL_handle_t *ssl, uint8_t *buf, int len)
 int SSLi_get_error(SSL_handle_t *ssl, int code)
 {
 	(void)ssl;
+	/* ESP-only: PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY -> ZERO_RETURN (see patch header). */
+	if (code == MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY)
+		return SSLI_ERROR_ZERO_RETURN;
 	return code;
 }
 
